{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites","id":477022,"title":"[From 1ED to 2ED] Lost Gifts and Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-11T09:07:35-07:00","id":477022,"title":"[From 1ED to 2ED] Lost Gifts and Rites","content":"So my players group is preparing to change our 1ED characters to the 2ED for the continuation of our chronicle. But there ae some powers missing in 2ED they acquired in 1ED. Will you help recreate them or change in to other powers?<br /> <br /> First problem is <i>Rite of Healing</i> ( WtF 1ED corebook, p. 159 ) our Ithaeur got from the powerful serpent spirit - is this Rite is useful anymore in 2ED? If yes, how would new <i>Rite of Healing </i>rules look like? If no, what 2ED alternative would you propose in it's place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:00:39-07:00","id":477088,"title":"","content":"Same, burn 2 essence per Aggy healed, would be a Wolf Rite, same rating and pick a theme and dice pool.<br /> <br /> Gonna lick your packmate's wounds while beseeching the spirits? Wits+Empathy.<br /> <br /> Gonna operate with blessed/anointed medical gear? Dexterity+Medicine.<br /> <br /> The list can go on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:06:00-07:00","id":477095,"title":"","content":"If your pack already went through a serious ordeal to get the Rite, I don't see any reason not to translate it fairly directly. Instead of Harmony, pick an Attribute + Skill dice pool. Rolls still take 15 minutes apiece, but you only get as many tries to roll as you have dice in your pool. If you don't hit your attempted target in the allotted time, the Rite fails, the Essence spent dissipates, and the target's regeneration is not supercharged and thus no special healing happens.<br /> As to symbols, I'd say cleansing, cycles, direction, and close ties.<br /> <br /> The Rite is still useful as aggravated damage otherwise takes 4 days per damage to heal and there's no other way around it. Even at the low end of this Rite, that's four times faster. The reason it was left out is to make aggravated damage seem like that much more of a big deal. I might still leave it out of the game, but since you've already had a reasonably big story to get it, I see no reason for your group to lose it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T21:12:37-07:00","id":477485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477088#post477088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same, burn 2 essence per Aggy healed, would be a Wolf Rite, same rating and pick a theme and dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not this be Pack Rite? But on the other hand, it's only help with regeneration abilities of Uratha. Would Wolf-Blooded with specific Tells ( like Wolf's Flesh ) could also benefit from it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477095#post477095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your pack already went through a serious ordeal to get the Rite, I don't see any reason not to translate it fairly directly. Instead of Harmony, pick an Attribute + Skill dice pool. Rolls still take 15 minutes apiece, but you only get as many tries to roll as you have dice in your pool. If you don't hit your attempted target in the allotted time, the Rite fails, the Essence spent dissipates, and the target's regeneration is not supercharged and thus no special healing happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not roll time is 10 minutes, as most Rites in 2ED have this time intervals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477088#post477088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to symbols, I'd say cleansing, cycles, direction, and close ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Licking should also not be a symbol here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477088#post477088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rite is still useful as aggravated damage otherwise takes 4 days per damage to heal and there's no other way around it. Even at the low end of this Rite, that's four times faster. The reason it was left out is to make aggravated damage seem like that much more of a big deal. I might still leave it out of the game, but since you've already had a reasonably big story to get it, I see no reason for your group to lose it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not Aggravated damage heals <b>one week</b> on normal rules? Why you mention it's only 4 days?<br /> <br /> So for this chronicle it's okay to get it. But on general, the Rite should not return to play in 2ED because of balance issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T21:31:43-07:00","id":477514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not Aggravated damage heals <b>one week</b> on normal rules? Why you mention it's only 4 days?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u20262e core. It's on one of the transposed pages, but at the moment it's page 95.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aggravated Damage: Aggravated damage regenerates much slower, closer to the speed of human wounds. Uratha heal one point of aggravated damage every four days. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T21:33:57-07:00","id":477519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should not this be Pack Rite? But on the other hand, it's only help with regeneration abilities of Uratha. Would Wolf-Blooded with specific Tells ( like Wolf's Flesh ) could also benefit from it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Should not roll time is 10 minutes, as most Rites in 2ED have this time intervals?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Licking should also not be a symbol here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Should not Aggravated damage heals <b>one week</b> on normal rules? Why you mention it's only 4 days?<br /> <br /> So for this chronicle it's okay to get it. But on general, the Rite should not return to play in 2ED because of balance issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean to be terse, but... If you already know how you want it to work, why are you asking for advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T22:21:00-07:00","id":477531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477514#post477514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u20262e core. It's on one of the transposed pages, but at the moment it's page 95.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so the 2ed Uratha heals Aggravated wounds quicker? Cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So it is a lower need for <i>Rite of Healing</i> now also, as Agg's are not so crippling now for PCs. I will use the transplanted Rite for now game, but will probably abandon it in loose continuation I plan for next year.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477519#post477519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean to be terse, but... If you already know how you want it to work, why are you asking for advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I put question marks after those statements not without a reason. Also, I observed I'm natural &quot;Devil's Advocate&quot; type of person - can do very good things when oppose other people opinions. Yeah, it's some how fae-ish, wyrd-ish thing in mine brain, as it seams. Also, I learn mechanics better, when I talk it over with others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you for the help to this point now. There are question that should be answered in remaking Rites from 1ED to 2ED:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Are symbols number generally set? Like there need to be 4 different symbols for each Rite?</li> <li>Rite have now unified roll intervals times?</li> <li>Wolf-Blooded can use the Uratha like regeneration supercharging - does it seems plausible in 2ED rules?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-12-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T22:23:50-07:00","id":477533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477531#post477531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, so the 2ed Uratha heals Aggravated wounds quicker? Cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So it is a lower need for <i>Rite of Healing</i> now also, as Agg's are not so crippling now for PCs. I will use the transplanted Rite for now game, but will probably abandon it in loose continuation I plan for next year.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I put question marks after those statements not without a reason. Also, I observed I'm natural &quot;Devil's Advocate&quot; type of person - can do very good things when oppose other people opinions. Yeah, it's some how fae-ish, wyrd-ish thing in mine brain, as it seams. Also, I learn mechanics better, when I talk it over with others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you for the help to this point now. There are question that should be answered in remaking Rites from 1ED to 2ED:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Are symbols number generally set? Like there need to be 4 different symbols each time?</li> <li>Rite have now unified roll intervals times?</li> <li>Wolf-Blooded can use the Uratha like regeneration supercharging - does it seems plausible in 2ED rules?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, cool. As long as the discussion is benefitting you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T23:25:13-07:00","id":477574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should not this be Pack Rite? But on the other hand, it's only help with regeneration abilities of Uratha. Would Wolf-Blooded with specific Tells ( like Wolf's Flesh ) could also benefit from it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pack Rite sounds better to me. If it's meant to improve natural Uratha healing, then I'd say it doesn't work Wolf-Blooded. Even one with A Wolf's Meat doesn't regenerate as quickly as a standard Uratha, being forced to use Willpower instead of Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not roll time is 10 minutes, as most Rites in 2ED have this time intervals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd stick with the original interval. Maybe even make it longer, since Agg is already healed more quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Licking should also not be a symbol here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the act of licking could be fulfill the <i>cleansing</i> symbol requirement, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not Aggravated damage heals <b>one week</b> on normal rules? Why you mention it's only 4 days?</div> </div> </div> </div>Already answered and you already answered back! :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477485#post477485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for this chronicle it's okay to get it. But on general, the Rite should not return to play in 2ED because of balance issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say balance issues. WoD is a lot more free-form with that kind of idea than lots of RPGs. In this case, I'd say part of the aesthetic was that WWs are total badasses, but part of that overconfidence can get them into trouble. See: Gauru heals <i>everything but Agg</i>, but can still be killed by overconfidence or stupidity.<br /> <br /> In 2e, part of the struggle may be that Agg damage can build up. PCs don't go into every situation with full health, which the Rite of Healing would facilitate (but not guarantee). Personally, I'd be against it, but it's your game and your PCs probably earned the Rite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T00:28:17-07:00","id":477628,"title":"","content":"Balance is a myth. Get over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T01:00:03-07:00","id":477656,"title":"","content":"What other powers do you need to convert?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T05:40:28-07:00","id":477848,"title":"","content":"On the Pack Rite or Wolf Rite question: Personally, I don't understand the distinction at all. They were split into two groups, but I don't know why, and am not sure it matters. There's that one little side bar about how some Wolf-Blooded (and maybe some other spirit attuned people) can perform Pack Rites. If that's the main distinction and the distinction matters to you, I'd say call it a Pack Rite. That way, one of your Wolf-Blooded could run it on wolves that had Essence available. Also, I do think someone with Wolf's Meat could benefit from this Rite as their body works in almost the same way. They just couldn't spend the Essence.<br /> For the rest of Wolf-Blooded, I'd leave it questionable. Maybe one of your people is up to all-but-one Agg and a bashing and you're in a semi-dangerous situation (but have an hour or so reprieve). The Rite is all you've got, see what happens... (So with this one, I'm running with the ideas from the Regeneration essay in the Storyteller section of the book on page 286. Stories get interesting when the rules are not so stable and set in stone)<br /> <br /> Four symbols per Rite is more a rule of thumb than anything. A quick perusal showed that a lot have four. Fetish has five. Four isn't a magical number, it's just plenty for guidance while still allowing you to come up with compelling, personalized Rites.<br /> <br /> On the Licking symbol Flailbot caught my drift. I think the original Rite suggested would licking or some other cleansing action, hence I suggested cleansing.<br /> <br /> I think Rite time intervals are more standardized now. I'm not sure where I saw this, though, so I don't have a page reference. That said, so long as the time interval is standardized for the Rite (and you're not just throwing a new interval at the players each time all willy-nilly) you should be fine.<br /> More than I remember seeing a chart for this sort of thing I remember the general Extended Action rules saying &quot;think about how long this sort of action should take overall and set the time scale based on that.&quot; From that perspective, the difference between 10 and 15 minutes doesn't mean a whole lot, unless you're in my aforementioned &quot;we've only got an hour before the shit hits the fan again&quot; scenario.<br /> <br /> Something I forgot to mention at first - Failed Rolls (no successes on one specific rolls) should probably offer the Stumbled Condition. Exceptional Success (overall) should grant the Uratha performing the Rite the Symbolic Focus Condition.<br /> <br /> Last thing: leaving this Rite out isn't so much a matter of Balance as it is an emphasis on the theme that, despite how powerful Werewolf regeneration is, there are still things out there that can mess you up right and proper. Aggravated damage is dangerous and will leave you screwed if you're not still careful. It might not be bad to have the Bale Hounds do something that makes the Rite not function anymore; maybe have a story in which the characters arive just as the Hounds are finishing some weird ritual, then have the Rite auto-fail next time they try to use it. Having this Rite and then losing it would really drive home the point. I'd apply Sanctity of Merits before too long, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T06:32:02-07:00","id":477862,"title":"","content":"For me it's a Wolf Rite because it'd only work on Uratha, and I'm not gonna have humans who could caught all sorta kinds of diseases licking someone's blood off.<br /> <br /> But I digress, it's not something I want regular humans having nearly any possibility to enact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:06:27-07:00","id":479048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=477862#post477862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's a Wolf Rite because it'd only work on Uratha, and I'm not gonna have humans who could caught all sorta kinds of diseases licking someone's blood off.<br /> But I digress, it's not something I want regular humans having nearly any possibility to enact.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Rite did have you licking wounds in 1st edition, but even then it wasn't the mandatory MO; it was just their recomended form of &quot;cleansing&quot;. What with the newer methods of Rite consctruction, anything that means &quot;cleansing&quot; to the ritemaster could work.<br /> <br /> And it wouldn't be a regular human. It would be someone who is a living locus, or someone who has a Tyler Durden spirit backing them up, or some other especially Hisil-tied person. More than anything, though, it would be a pack mate.<br /> <br /> Edit: so is that the only distinction between Wolf Rites and Pack Rites? Pack Rites could, potentially, be done by Wolf-Blooded but Wolf Rites cannot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:16:46-07:00","id":479058,"title":"","content":"Pack rites also include things that affect the whole pack, humans included, such as the one the turns every non-werewolf into a wolf for one night so everyone can go hunting together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:21:40-07:00","id":479063,"title":"","content":"Then why are Banish and Shadowcall Pack Rites, and why is Forge Alliance a Wolf Rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:40:03-07:00","id":479075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/477022-from-1ed-to-2ed-lost-gifts-and-rites?p=479063#post479063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why are Banish and Shadowcall Pack Rites, and why is Forge Alliance a Wolf Rite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forge Alliance is a Wolf Rite because Pack Rites only work with participants from the same pack and <i>the </i><i><i>entire</i> purpose of Forge Alliance is to merge two or more packs.</i><br /> <br /> Banish and Shadowcall are Pack Rites because those rites can empower non-werewolf characters and because summoning and banishing are rather high on the go-to list of Ritual Activities With Multiple Participants. Elfive's &quot;Pack Rites also include\u2026&quot; should not be taken as &quot;Pack Rites consist entirely of\u2026&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:54:31-07:00","id":479138,"title":"","content":"Okay, that all makes sense. Given that Pack Rites are expected to include most or all of the pack, should you use teamwork rules? Or is part of the reason they're called out as different from Wolf Rites that the expectation of the inclusion of help pre-empts the use of teamwork rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:05:01-07:00","id":479165,"title":"","content":"As the rules on rites state:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any Uratha who knows a rite may lead it as a ritemaster.<br /> Other characters who know the rite may aid her as a teamwork<br /> action. Uratha from different packs can come together to<br /> perform a Wolf Rite, but Pack Rites require all participants<br /> to be from the same pack. Pack Rites can also involve pack<br /> members who do not know the rite itself. These participants<br /> do not contribute any teamwork bonus but may benefit from<br /> the rite\u2019s effects. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:48:08-07:00","id":479184,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Chris!<br /> <br /> So in that case, the question becomes whether you want to allow someone from outside your pack to wash your wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T16:17:50-07:00","id":479590,"title":"","content":"I do, pretty much. Nevermind that the rite wouldn't actually work with the human beings member of packs, as it needs to supercharge regeneration. Not pack rite material for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:54:03-07:00","id":481331,"title":"","content":"If you can make a Medicine roll to convert a Human's Aggravated to Lethal (is that still a thing in 2nd Edition?), I see no reason the Rite would not work. Just sayin' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 04-15-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T09:26:53-07:00","id":481367,"title":"","content":"Plus some wolf blooded <i>do</i> regenerate like a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}